2026-09-15T20:36Z claude note CORRECTION to this ticket's 20:34Z entry, which is append-only and therefore stands wrong above: toggling off/on is NOT the escape hatch from ticket 0796's drain starvation. The concurrent sitter session measured it from `sdt-sitter-last-shutdown.json` across two real off/on cycles (20:16:55 and 20:22:53) and the record splits in two. What the toggle DOES do, and what this ticket's invariant now protects, is force a fresh census within two seconds of each `on`, and that census works: `failed` fell 13 749 -> 5 242 and `pending` rose 436 -> 8 926 as attachments whose files had landed left `missing-source`. What it does NOT do is restart the pump: each census was followed by a `drain-start` of ~9 600 dirty ids, after which `pending` froze and `active` stayed null, seven minutes the second time, and BOTH `sweep-end` records carry `completed: 0` -- 8 926 admissible candidates, not one submitted, nothing indexed all session. The starvation is also not permanent: between 20:08 and 20:15 `pending` rose 44 -> 389, which only happens if `refreshQueue()` ran, so the drain had emptied when the notification source dried up. Dossier: verification/incidents/0796-2026-09-15-toggle-does-not-recover.md. Two attributions in that session's reading are corrected here: the toggles and the 20:31:54Z uninstall were NOT this session's doing -- this session has no console on the live Zotero instance and touched neither -- so whoever took those actions is unidentified by anything either session measured, and the incident record should not name one.
